## Usage

### Basic
Semantic `type` values provide numeric sorting, tag pills, and local calendar dates; `filter: true` adds the matching header filter.
::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="DataTableDataTableDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  const columns = [
    { key: 'name', title: 'Name' },
    { key: 'role', title: 'Role', type: 'tag', filter: true },
    { key: 'score', title: 'Score', type: 'number', filter: true },
    { key: 'joinedAt', title: 'Joined', type: 'date', filter: true },
  ]

  const data = [
    { id: 1, name: 'Ava', role: 'Designer', score: 92, joinedAt: '2026-10-14' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Noah', role: 'Engineer', score: 88, joinedAt: '2026-10-13' },
    { id: 3, name: 'Mia', role: 'PM', score: 95, joinedAt: '2026-10-12' },
  ]
  </script>

  <template>
    <TxDataTable :columns="columns" :data="data" striped bordered />
  </template>
---
::

### Sorting
Number and date columns sort on their own, other columns opt in with `sortable`; `defaultSort` sets the starting order, and `sortCycle` decides whether a third click unsorts.
::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="DataTableSortingDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  const columns = [
    { key: 'title', title: 'Track', sortable: true },
    { key: 'artist', title: 'Artist' },
    { key: 'duration', title: 'Length', type: 'number', format: formatDuration },
    { key: 'plays', title: 'Plays', type: 'number' },
    { key: 'releasedAt', title: 'Released', type: 'date' },
  ]
  </script>

  <template>
    <TxDataTable
      :columns="columns"
      :data="rows"
      row-key="id"
      :default-sort="{ key: 'plays', order: 'desc' }"
      sort-cycle="bi"
      @update:sort="sort = $event"
    />
  </template>
---
::

### Filtering
`filter: true` gives each column the filter its type calls for: text search, tag picks, a number range, or date presets; a `filter-<key>` slot swaps in a panel of your own, and `v-model:filter` hands the state to the parent.
::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="DataTableFiltersDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  const filter = ref({})

  const columns = [
    { key: 'title', title: 'Track', filter: true },
    { key: 'artist', title: 'Artist', type: 'tag', filter: true },
    { key: 'duration', title: 'Length', type: 'number', filter: true },
    { key: 'plays', title: 'Plays', type: 'number', filter: true },
    { key: 'updatedAt', title: 'Updated', type: 'datetime', filter: true },
  ]

  // A preset writes the { min, max } shape a number column already filters by.
  const RANGES = { short: { max: 180 }, mid: { min: 180, max: 240 }, long: { min: 240 } }
  </script>

  <template>
    <TxDataTable v-model:filter="filter" :columns="columns" :data="rows" :labels="labels" row-key="id">
      <template #filter-duration="{ filterValue, setFilter, close }">
        <TxFlatRadio
          :model-value="bucketOf(filterValue)"
          @update:model-value="value => { setFilter(RANGES[value]); close() }"
        >
          <TxFlatRadioItem value="all" label="All" />
          <TxFlatRadioItem value="short" label="Under 3 min" />
          <TxFlatRadioItem value="mid" label="3–4 min" />
          <TxFlatRadioItem value="long" label="Over 4 min" />
        </TxFlatRadio>
      </template>
    </TxDataTable>
  </template>
---
::

### Row Selection
`selectable` adds a selection column; `v-model:selected-keys` syncs the selected rows.
::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="DataTableDataTableSelectableDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <TxDataTable
      v-model:selected-keys="selectedKeys"
      :columns="columns"
      :data="data"
      row-key="id"
      selectable
    />
  </template>
---
::

### Expandable Rows
`expandable` adds a leading toggle column; the `#expanded` slot renders the detail under a row.
::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="DataTableExpandableRowsDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <TxDataTable
      v-model:expanded-keys="expandedKeys"
      :columns="columns"
      :data="data"
      row-key="id"
      expandable
      :row-expandable="row => Boolean(row.note)"
    >
      <template #expanded="{ row }">
        {{ row.note }}
      </template>
    </TxDataTable>
  </template>
---
::

### Adaptive Column Widths
A nowrap column without a declared width hugs its content and the others share what is left; the action column pins right by default, and the table scrolls once nothing fits.
::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="DataTableColumnWidthsDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  // No column declares a width; the one that wraps gets a floor.
  const columns = [
    { key: 'code', title: 'Code', fixed: 'left', nowrap: true },
    { key: 'title', title: 'Track', minWidth: 160 },
    { key: 'artist', title: 'Artist', type: 'tag' },
    { key: 'plays', title: 'Plays', type: 'number' },
    { key: 'source', title: 'Source', type: 'source' },
    { key: 'actions', title: 'Actions' },
  ]
  </script>

  <template>
    <TxDataTable :columns="columns" :data="rows" row-key="id" selectable scroll-x>
      <template #cell-actions>
        <TxButton variant="secondary" size="sm">Edit</TxButton>
        <TxIconButton icon="i-carbon-overflow-menu-horizontal" size="sm" label="More" />
      </template>
    </TxDataTable>
  </template>
---
::

### Loading States
`loadingVariant` picks a veil, skeleton rows, or a shimmer; skeleton and shimmer draw placeholder rows only while there are none, and a refresh keeps the existing rows.
::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="DataTableSkeletonLoadingDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <!-- variant: 'overlay' | 'skeleton' | 'shimmer' -->
    <TxDataTable
      :columns="columns"
      :data="rows"
      :loading="loading"
      :loading-variant="variant"
      :skeleton-rows="pageSize"
      row-key="id"
    />
  </template>
---
::

### Empty State
The `#empty` slot replaces the empty state of a table with no rows, with room for an explanation and an action; to change only the text, pass `emptyText`.
::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="DataTableEmptyStateDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <TxDataTable :columns="columns" :data="visibleRows" row-key="id">
      <template #empty>
        <TxEmptyState
          variant="search-empty"
          size="small"
          :title="`No tracks match “${query}”`"
          :primary-action="{ label: 'Clear search', variant: 'secondary' }"
          @primary="query = ''"
        />
      </template>
    </TxDataTable>
  </template>
---
::

### Records Table
A wide layout with a pinned header and footer, a frozen first column, and selection highlighting; cells compose `TxTag`, `TxDotIndicator`, and `TxCellLink`.
::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="DataTableRecordsDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <TxDataTable
      v-model:selected-keys="selectedKeys"
      :columns="columns"
      :data="rows"
      :sort="sort"
      row-key="id"
      selectable
      highlight-selected
      table-layout="fixed"
      nowrap
      sort-cycle="bi"
      :max-height="380"
      scroll-x
      sticky-header
      sticky-footer
      @update:sort="sort = $event"
    >
      <template #cell-tags="{ value }">
        <TxTag v-for="tag in value" :key="tag" :label="tag" :dot="TAG_COLORS[tag]" variant="soft" />
      </template>
      <template #cell-strength="{ row }">
        <TxDotIndicator :color="STRENGTH_TONE[row.strength]" :label="STRENGTH_LABEL[row.strength]" />
      </template>
      <template #cell-website="{ value }">
        <TxCellLink :href="`https://${value}`" :label="value" external @open="openSite" />
      </template>

      <template #footer-name>
        <strong>{{ rows.length }}</strong> count
      </template>
      <template #footer-website>
        {{ linkCount }} links
      </template>
    </TxDataTable>
  </template>
---
::

### Data Operations Panel
`TxPagination` pages the list, and `TxSkeleton` / `TxLayoutSkeleton` preview the loading state.
::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="ComponentsDataOperationsDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <TxDataTable
      v-model:selected-keys="selectedKeys"
      :columns="columns"
      :data="pagedRows"
      row-key="id"
      selectable
      striped
      bordered
    />
    <TxPagination v-model:current-page="page" :total="rows.length" :page-size="4" show-info />
  </template>
---
::

### Best Practices

- Pass a stable `rowKey` for business lists; to keep selection across pages, drive `selectedKeys` with business ids, not default indexes.
- For server-loaded lists, use `loadingVariant="skeleton"` or `"shimmer"` with `skeletonRows` set to the page size; keep the default `overlay` for short local waits.
- Let content size the columns: a nowrap column hugs its content with no declared width, and a long wrapping column takes a `minWidth` as the floor it wraps to.
- Fixed-column offsets are measured from the rendered widths; give numeric `width`s only when several columns pin to one side, so the first frame and server render line up. Keep one horizontal scroller: `scrollX`, or an outer `overflow-x: auto`.
- A pinned header or footer needs `maxHeight` or a scrolling ancestor; don't nest the table in `TxScroll`'s default mode, whose transform scrolling disables sticky.
- Sort on comparable fields such as timestamps or ranks, never on formatted relative-time text.
- Use `filterOnClient=false` for remote filtering and handle `filterChange` alongside pagination, passing tag-option row counts as `count` in `filterOptions`; controlled `filter` remains the parent's state.
- The filter controls speak English by default; localize them through `labels`, whose keys `DATA_TABLE_DEFAULT_LABELS` lists.
- A `date` column interprets `YYYY-MM-DD` as a local calendar day. A `datetime` column preserves the instant of timezone-qualified values; `today` ends at the next local midnight, including daylight-saving transitions.

## API Reference

### Props

| Name | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|------|------|
| `columns` | `DataTableColumn[]` | `[]` | Column config. |
| `data` | `any[]` | `[]` | Data source. |
| `rowKey` | `keyof T \| (row: T, index: number) => string \| number` | `index` | Unique row key. |
| `loading` | `boolean` | `false` | Loading state. |
| `loadingVariant` | `'overlay' \| 'skeleton' \| 'shimmer'` | `'overlay'` | `overlay` veils the table with a spinner; `skeleton` draws placeholder rows, or only a bar when rows exist; `shimmer` sweeps a band of light across the placeholder rows or the existing ones. |
| `skeletonRows` | `number` | `5` | Placeholder rows `skeleton` and `shimmer` draw before the first data lands; match the page size so nothing moves. A table whose host sets its height fills it to the bottom. |
| `emptyText` | `string` | `'No data'` | Empty text. |
| `striped` | `boolean` | `false` | Zebra rows. |
| `bordered` | `boolean` | `false` | Show borders. |
| `hover` | `boolean` | `true` | Hover highlight. |
| `interactiveRows` | `boolean` | `false` | Makes rows focusable so Enter / Space fire `rowClick`; on automatically with a `rowClick` listener. |
| `selectable` | `boolean` | `false` | Adds a selection column. |
| `selectedKeys` | `Array<string \| number>` | `[]` | Keys of the selected rows. |
| `expandable` | `boolean` | `false` | Adds a leading toggle column; an expanded row renders a detail row beneath it. |
| `defaultExpandedKeys` | `Array<string \| number>` | `[]` | Initial expanded rows when uncontrolled; `expandedKeys` wins if both are passed. |
| `expandedKeys` | `Array<string \| number>` | - | Controlled expanded rows, bound with `v-model:expanded-keys`. |
| `rowExpandable` | `(row, index) => boolean` | - | Per-row gate for expanding; a rejected row keeps an empty leading cell. |
| `expandLabel` | `string` | `'Expand row'` | Accessible name of a closed toggle. |
| `collapseLabel` | `string` | `'Collapse row'` | Accessible name of an open toggle. |
| `defaultSort` | `{ key: string; order: 'asc' \| 'desc' \| null }` | `null` | Initial sort when uncontrolled; pass either this or `sort`. |
| `sort` | `{ key: string; order: 'asc' \| 'desc' \| null } \| null` | - | Controlled sort; `null` means unsorted. |
| `sortOnClient` | `boolean` | `true` | Sorts locally; set `false` for remote sorting, which only emits. |
| `sortCycle` | `'tri' \| 'bi'` | `'tri'` | `tri`: ascending → descending → unsorted; `bi` alternates and never unsorts. |
| `tableLayout` | `'auto' \| 'fixed'` | `'auto'` | Native `table-layout`; use `fixed` when column widths must stay stable. |
| `nowrap` | `boolean` | `false` | Prevents wrapping in every header and cell. |
| `maxHeight` | `string \| number` | - | Caps the height and scrolls the table vertically; what sticky rows stick to. |
| `scrollX` | `boolean` | `false` | Scrolls horizontally inside the component; for wide tables with fixed columns. |
| `stickyHeader` | `boolean` | `false` | Pins the header row. |
| `stickyFooter` | `boolean` | `false` | Pins the summary row. |
| `rowClass` | `(row, index) => string \| string[] \| Record<string, boolean>` | - | Extra classes per row, such as a tint by state. |
| `highlightSelected` | `boolean` | `false` | Tints selected rows. |
| `defaultFilter` | `DataTableFilterState` | `{}` | Initial filter values in uncontrolled mode. |
| `filter` | `DataTableFilterState` | - | Controlled values by column key; bind with `v-model:filter`. |
| `filterOnClient` | `boolean` | `true` | Filters rows locally; `false` delegates row retrieval to the caller. |
| `autoStickyActions` | `boolean` | `true` | Defaults action columns to the right fixed edge; an explicit column `fixed` takes precedence. |
| `labels` | `Partial<DataTableLabels>` | - | Text of the filter controls; pass only the keys to replace, the rest keep their English defaults. |

### Events

| Event | Payload | Description |
|------|------|------|
| `update:selectedKeys` | `(keys)` | Selection update. |
| `selectionChange` | `(keys)` | Selection change. |
| `update:expandedKeys` | `(keys)` | Expansion update; fires in controlled and uncontrolled modes. |
| `expand` | `({ row, index, expanded })` | A row was expanded or collapsed. |
| `sortChange` | `(sort)` | Sort change. |
| `update:sort` | `(sort)` | Sort change; fires in controlled and uncontrolled modes. |
| `update:filter` | `(filter)` | Filter values changed; fires in controlled and uncontrolled modes. |
| `filterChange` | `(filter)` | Filter changes for client or remote filtering. |
| `rowClick` | `({ row, index })` | Row click. |

### Slots

| Name | Description |
|------|------|
| `header-<columnKey>` | Custom header; receives `{ column, sorted, order, toggle }`, where `toggle` advances the sort cycle. |
| `cell-<columnKey>` | Custom cell; receives `{ row, column, value, index }`. |
| `filter-<columnKey>` | Custom filter panel; receives `{ column, filterValue, setFilter, clearFilter, close }`, where `close` closes the panel. |
| `expanded` | Detail of an expanded row, spanning every column; receives `{ row, index }`. |
| `footer` | The whole summary row of your own `<td>`s, which can span columns. Any footer slot renders a `<tfoot>`. |
| `footer-<columnKey>` | One summary cell per column; receives `{ column, data }`. `footer` wins when both exist. |
| `empty` | Empty state when there are no rows and `loading=false`. |

### DataTableColumn

| Field | Type | Description |
|------|------|------|
| `key` | `string` | Column key. |
| `title` | `string` | Header title. |
| `type` | `'text' \| 'number' \| 'datetime' \| 'date' \| 'tag' \| 'source' \| 'actions'` | Semantic display, sort, and filter behavior; cell slots and `format` take precedence. |
| `dataIndex` | `string` | Data field. |
| `width` | `string \| number` | Column width. Left out, a nowrap column hugs its content and the others share what is left. |
| `minWidth` | `string \| number` | Minimum column width. |
| `maxWidth` | `string \| number` | Maximum column width. |
| `auto` | `boolean` | Forces the column width to `auto`. |
| `fixed` | `boolean \| 'left' \| 'right'` | Sticky side; `true` means `'left'`. Offsets are measured from the rendered widths, and left ones include the toggle and selection columns. |
| `nowrap` | `boolean` | Prevents wrapping in this column. |
| `align` | `'left' \| 'center' \| 'right'` | Alignment. |
| `sortable` | `boolean` | Sortable. |
| `sorter` | `(a, b) => number` | Custom sorter. |
| `filter` | `boolean` | Adds a type-aware header filter; off by default. |
| `filterOptions` | `DataTableFilterOption[]` | Custom tag-filter options containing `label`, `value`, and optional `tone` and `count` (the row count shown beside the option). |
| `format` | `(value, row, index) => string` | Cell formatter. |
| `headerClass` | `string` | Header class. |
| `cellClass` | `string` | Cell class. |

### DataTableLabels

| Key | Default | Description |
|------|------|------|
| `filter` | `'Filter {column}'` | Accessible name of a filter button; `{column}` becomes the column title. |
| `filterAll` | `'All'` | Option that clears a tag filter. |
| `filterAnyTime` | `'Any time'` | Option that clears a date filter. |
| `filterToday` | `'Today'` | Date preset: today. |
| `filterLast3Days` | `'Last 3 days'` | Date preset: the last 3 days. |
| `filterLast7Days` | `'Last 7 days'` | Date preset: the last 7 days. |
| `filterLast30Days` | `'Last 30 days'` | Date preset: the last 30 days. |
| `filterSearch` | `'Search'` | Placeholder of the text filter and of a long tag list's search field. |
| `filterMin` | `'Min'` | Lower bound of a number range. |
| `filterMax` | `'Max'` | Upper bound of a number range. |
| `filterReset` | `'Reset'` | Clears a number range. |
| `filterApply` | `'Done'` | Closes a number range. |

## Overview

- Passing `sort` or `expandedKeys` (even `null` or `[]`) makes it controlled: the table only emits updates and renders what the parent sends back.
- `filter` also makes filtering controlled. Tags accept one value or multiple values, numbers accept `{ min, max }`, and dates accept `today`, `3d`, `7d`, `30d`, or timestamp `{ start, end }` values. Text columns match a case-insensitive substring.
- When a tag filter gathers its options from the rows, client filtering counts the rows behind each one; at 8 options the panel gains a search field.
- Sortable headers carry `scope="col"` and `aria-sort`; click, Enter, and Space step through `sortCycle`.
- On a partial selection the select-all box is `indeterminate` (`aria-checked="mixed"`); clicks in the selection and toggle cells never fire `rowClick`.
- `loading` sets `aria-busy` on the `<table>`, and the empty state stays hidden while loading. `overlay` covers only the visible part of the table, and a table with no rows keeps the height of its empty state.
- Placeholder rows are `aria-hidden` and as tall as a one-line row. Under reduced motion the refresh bar holds still and the shimmer becomes a still wash.
- `stickyHeader`, `stickyFooter`, or `maxHeight` switches to `border-collapse: separate`. The last row has no bottom rule; the rule above a `tfoot` stays.

## Technologies

- The skeleton variant renders `TxSkeleton`. The on-demand style plugin loads its sheet; when importing styles by hand, add `@talex-touch/tuffex/skeleton/style.css`.
- Semantic defaults, filtering, and sorting share the internal `useDataTableData` module; the internal `useDataTableLayout` measures column widths, fixed-column offsets, the veil's height, and the shimmer bands.
- Tag and date filters use `TxDropdownMenu` / `TxDropdownItem`, number and text filters use `TxPopover`; the teleported panels keep component-owned BEM styling.
- Source: `packages/tuffex/packages/components/src/data-table/`.

